#: rc.cpp:5398
#, kde-format
msgid "Set the curve radius in dB for all joints."
msgstr "Establix el radi de corba en dB per a totes les unions."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5402
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Set the additional gain in dB to be applied at all points on the transfer "
"function. This allows for easy adjustment of the overall gain."
msgstr ""
"Establix el guany addicional en dB que s'aplicarà en tots els punts de la "
"funció de transferència. Açò permet un ajust fàcil del guany general."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5404
#, kde-format
msgid "Initial volume"
msgstr "Volum inicial"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compand.xml
#: rc.cpp:5406
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Set an initial volume, in dB, to be assumed for each channel when filtering "
"starts. This permits the user to supply a nominal level initially, so that, "
"for example, a very large gain is not applied to initial signal levels "
"before the companding has begun to operate. A typical value for audio which "
"is initially quiet is -90 dB."
msgstr ""
"Establix un volum inicial, en dB, que s'assumirà per a cada canal quan "
"s'inicie el filtratge. Açò permet a l'usuari subministrar inicialment un "
"nivell nominal, de manera que, per exemple, un guany molt gran no s'aplica "
"als nivells inicials del senyal abans que la combinació haja començat a "
"funcionar. Un valor típic per a l'àudio que inicialment és silenciós és -90 "
"dB."

#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compensationdelay.xml
#: rc.cpp:5408
#, kde-format
msgid "Compensation Delay"
msgstr "Retard de compensació"

# skip-rule: common-diferent_a
#. i18n: file: data/effects/avfilter/avfilter_compensationdelay.xml
#: rc.cpp:5410
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Compensation Delay Line is a metric based delay to compensate differing "
#| "positions of microphones or speakers.\n"
#| "For example, you have recorded guitar with two microphones placed in "
#| "different locations. Because the front of sound wave has fixed speed in "
#| "normal conditions, the phasing of microphones can vary and depends on "
#| "their location and interposition. The best sound mix can be achieved when "
#| "these microphones are in phase (synchronized). Note that a distance of "
#| "~30 cm between microphones makes one microphone capture the signal in "
#| "antiphase to the other microphone. That makes the final mix sound moody. "
#| "This filter helps to solve phasing problems by adding different delays to "
#| "each microphone track and make them synchronized.\n"
#| "\n"
#| "The best result can be reached when you take one track as base and "
#| "synchronize other tracks one by one with it. Remember that "
#| "synchronization/delay tolerance depends on sample rate, too. Higher "
#| "sample rates will give more tolerance. "
msgid ""
"Compensation Delay Line is a metric based delay to compensate differing "
"positions of microphones or speakers.\n"
"For example, you have recorded guitar with two microphones placed in "
"different locations. Because the front of sound wave has fixed speed in "
"normal conditions, the phasing of microphones can vary and depends on their "
"location and interposition. The best sound mix can be achieved when these "
"microphones are in phase (synchronized). Note that a distance of ~30 cm "
"between microphones makes one microphone capture the signal in antiphase to "
"the other microphone. That makes the final mix sound moody. This filter "
"helps to solve phasing problems by adding different delays to each "
"microphone track and make them synchronized.\n"
"\n"
"The best result can be reached when you take one track as base and "
"synchronize other tracks one by one with it. Remember that synchronization/"
"delay tolerance depends on sample rate, too. Higher sample rates will give "
"more tolerance."
msgstr ""
"La compensació de retard de línia és un retard basat en una distància "
"mètrica per a compensar les posicions diferents dels micròfons o altaveus.\n"
"Per exemple, heu gravat la guitarra amb dos micròfons col·locats en "
"ubicacions diferents. Com que la part davantera de l'ona sonora té una "
"velocitat fixa en condicions normals, la fase dels micròfons pot variar i "
"depén de la seua ubicació i interposició. La millor mescla de so es pot "
"aconseguir quan estos micròfons estan en fase (sincronitzats). Cal tindre en "
"compte que una distància de ~30 cm entre micròfons fa que un micròfon capti "
"el senyal en antifase amb l'altre micròfon. Açò fa que la mescla final sone "
"malament. Este filtre ajuda a resoldre problemes de fase afegint retards "
"diferents a cada pista de micròfon i sincronitzant-los.\n"
"\n"
"El resultat millor es pot aconseguir quan agafeu una pista com a base i "
"sincronitzeu altres pistes una a una amb ella. Recordeu que la tolerància a "
"la sincronització/retard també depén de la freqüència de mostreig. Les taxes "
"de mostreig més altes donaran més tolerància."

